# Step 21.26 (b): the kernel's list of the words of the language and the one predicate that P0 and the kernel share. Written from the texts BEFORE the slice (the old literal of
# lmx_graph_receivers_in, the profile unit and receiver-table.tsv measured with the accepted Graph), not from a run of the new kernel:
#   - state\receivers holds 109 words in this order: fn sub fm, the other 46 words of the literal, the 25 non-empty C names, the 35 names of the primitive profile;
#   - lmx_language_call_word(text) is 1 for a word that P0 reads as a CALL and 0 for a declaration (fn, sub, fm, a primitive name with an unset cell, a user name);
#   - lmx_graph_language_receiver(interned word) is 1 for a word of the kernel's list, a C name and a primitive name with a set cell -- fn, sub, fm among them -- and 0 for the rest.
# Entry 7; the codes 1000+ name the failing word of the order, 2000+ the failing word of the table (call_word), 3000+ the failing word of the table (receiver).
predef: "l2src/lmx_graph.h.lm1"
predef: "l2src/lmx_language_words.h.lm1"
include: "<string.h>"

fn: gw_call (@: word char) int
    return: c.lmx_language_call_word(word, c.strlen(word))
end: gw_call

fn: gw_receiver (@: word char) int
    return: c.lmx_graph_language_receiver(c.lmx_graph_intern(word, c.strlen(word)))
end: gw_receiver

fn: gw_call_word_check () int
    @: state c.LmxGraphState c.lmx_graph_state()
    if: state = 0
        return: 1
    if: state\receivers_count != 109U
        return: 2
    if: state\receivers[0U] != c.lmx_graph_intern("fn", 2U)
        return: 1000
    if: state\receivers[1U] != c.lmx_graph_intern("sub", 3U)
        return: 1001
    if: state\receivers[2U] != c.lmx_graph_intern("fm", 2U)
        return: 1002
